QuestGuidance.Register("en",230,{
[7329]="7003FD6C\n1\tTalk to Waldere\tWaldere is in the tunnel before you, injured and exhausted.\n2\tTalk to Waldere and declare your intentions\tWaldere has asked if you plan to venture deeper into the Paths of the Dead by yourself or if you have a Fellowship near at hand.\n3\tSearch the south-west tunnel in the Paths of the Dead for Elfdag\tWaldere told you that his men were slain outside of a passage in the south-west of a cavernous chamber, and thinks you should search that tunnel for Elfdag.\n4\tFight off the Dead Men and rescue Elfdag\tA great city of the Dead stands beneath the mountains. You have found Elfdag in the Paths of the Dead, and now must fight to free him from the Dead.\n5\tTalk to Elfdag in the Paths of the Dead\tElfdag is in the empty streets of the city of the Dead beneath the mountains.\n",
[7330]="7005B252\n1\tTalk to Hórin\tHórin is ready to stop the ritual taking place in Bagud-dum. You should talk to Hórin.\n2\tDefeat the approaching fell spirits\tThe Angmarim are attempting a ritual that will empower Loknashra! You should defeat the approaching fell spirits!\n3\tDefeat the Angmarim cultists\tThe Angmarim are attempting a ritual that will empower Loknashra! You should defeat the cultists performing the ritual!\n",
[7331]="70018F15\n1\tTalk to Orvar in Zurr-thurkh\tNo one has walked the 'secret road' since before the Fall of Moria, but now you and Orvar Bellhammer will use it to get behind the walls of Mazog's fortress, Zabadgathol.\n2\tClear the way ahead for Orvar\tYou should clear the way for Orvar to follow when he is ready.\n3\tTalk to Orvar in Rushdurinul\tOrvar is waiting outside the secret road, in Rushdurinul.\n4\tSearch the Orc encampment for Bori\tOrvar has told you to search the large Orc encampment in the throne room for the captive Bori.\n5\tTalk to Orvar\tWith no sign of Bori in the Orc encampment within Rushdurinul, Orvar has decided to confront Mazog directly.\n6\tProtect Orvar as he confronts Mazog\tYou have come with Orvar to Rushdurinul, the throne room in which Mazog makes his lair, and will now confront the Orc leader.\n7\tTalk to Bróin\030Talk to Corunothiel\tWith the sudden appearance of Bróin and the Elves from Buzun-ghâr, Mazog has been defeated.\n",
[7332]="70055185\n1\tTalk to Mithrandir\tMithrandir can be found in Falch Gurth.\n2\tFollow Mithrandir\tYou and Mithrandir are walking through Falch Gurth.\n3\tAllow Mithrandir to banish the shadows in Falch Gurth\tYou are following Mithrandir.\n4\tTalk to Mithrandir\tYou should talk to Mithrandir.\n5\tFollow Mithrandir\tYou are following Mithrandir.\n6\tAllow Mithrandir to banish the shadows in Falch Gurth\tYou are following Mithrandir.\n7\tTalk to Mithrandir\tYou should talk to Mithrandir.\n8\tFollow Mithrandir\tYou should follow Mithrandir.\n9\tAllow Mithrandir to banish the shadows of Thuringwath\tYou are following Mithrandir.\n10\tTalk to Mithrandir\tYou should talk to Mithrandir.\n",
[7333]="7004E72D\n1\tDefend yourself against the dragon-kind!\tDefend yourself against the dragon-kind.\n2\tTalk to the dwarf\tYou should speak with the dwarf.\n",
[7334]="700571AF\n1\tApproach the dwarves\tApproach the dwarves.\n2\tLet events transpire\tLet events transpire.\n3\tDefeat Rákhrum and his forces\tDefeat Rákhrum and his forces. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[7335]="70052E2D\n1\tTalk to Baradal\tBaradal is standing by outside Shathur-munzu. You should talk to Baradal.\n2\tDefeat the attacker\tYou find yourself inside a cage in Shathur-munzu. You should wake up.\n3\tKnock out the Orc jailor\tAn Orc has approached your cage, taunting you. You should knock out the Orc.\n",
[7336]="7003FDE3\n1\tTalk to Rovalang\tYou have come to the foothills of the White Mountains in the company of Rovalang, searching for the terrible beast he saw flying above the Blackroot Vale.\n2\tTalk to Rovalang and declare your intentions\tRovalang has asked if you and he are on your own, or if you have a Fellowship near at hand.\n3\tClimb the slope and stop the Nazgûl from learning of Aragorn's passage. Rovalang must not be defeated.\tYou must find the Nazgûl and prevent it from learning of Aragorn's passage. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tDefeat the Nazgûl before Drugât emerges from the Paths of the Dead. Rovalang must not be defeated.\tIf the Nazgûl is able to learn of Aragorn's passage, the Ranger's advantage will be lost. You must defeat the Nazgûl before he can meet with Drugât! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n5\tTalk to Rovalang\tRovalang is waiting to speak with you.\n",
[7337]="70053B91\n1\tTalk to Lethi\tLethi can be found near Hakal-kúnug, the Twisted Stair within Barad-dûr. You should talk to Lethi.\n2\tFollow Lethi\tLethi can be found near Hakal-kúnug, the Twisted Stair within Barad-dûr. You should follow Lethi and find your way to the gates of Barad-dûr.\n3\tTalk to Ashaug\tAshaug can be found near Hakal-kúnug, the Twisted Stair within Barad-dûr. Ashaug has sustained a grave wound in the fighting within Barad-dûr, but his wounds seem to be inflicted by an unusual source. You should talk to Ashaug.\n4\tCollect an abandoned weapon to defend yourself\tAbandoned weapons can be found near the slain Orcs near Hakal-kúnug, the Twisted Stair within Barad-dûr. You should find a suitable weapon with which to defend yourself before pressing on through Barad-dûr.\n5\tTalk to Lethi\tLethi can be found in Barad-dûr. You have taken a weapon. You should talk to Lethi and follow him to the gates of Barad-dûr.\n6\tFollow Lethi\tLethi can be found in Barad-dûr. Lethi is pressing on to the gates of Barad-dûr. You should follow him.\n7\tThe pale creature can be found in Barad-dûr. Despite appearing to be dead, the pale creature has scrambled to its feet and attacked Lethi. You should defend him and drive off the creature.\t\n8\tTalk to Lethi\tLethi can be found in Barad-dûr. After repelling the pale creature that attacked him, Lethi is shaken. You should talk to Lethi before pressing on to the gates of Barad-dûr.\n9\tFollow Lethi\tLethi has travelled into the shadowed halls of Barad-dûr. You should follow Lethi and press on to the gates of Barad-dûr.\n10\tTalk to Lethi\tLethi can be found Barad-dûr. Lethi is standing next to a brazier in Barad-dûr. You should talk to Lethi.\n11\tFollow Lethi\tLethi can be found in Barad-dûr. Lethi is pressing on toward the gates of Barad-dûr. You should follow him.\n12\tDisguise yourself as an Orc-captain\tThe slain Orc-captain can be found just ahead of Lethi in Barad-dûr. After spying a slain Orc-captain, Lethi has urged you to disguise yourself in its armour so that you might fool the inhabitants of Mordor. You should disguise yourself.\n13\tTalk to Lethi\tLethi can be found in Barad-dûr. You have disguised yourself as an Orc-captain, which may be of help in escaping the Land of Mordor. You should talk to Lethi.\n14\tPeer around the corner and look to see if the gates of Barad-dûr are unguarded\tThe path to the gates of Barad-dûr is just ahead of you. Lethi has asked you to peer around the corner and see if the path out of Barad-dûr is clear.\n15\tTalk to Lethi\tLethi can be found in Barad-dûr. You discovered the uruk, Ushgrat, guarding the gates of Barad-dûr. Worse still, he appears to have subdued Vaski. You should talk to Lethi.\n16\tConfront the Uruk\tAfter foiling Vaski's escape, Ushgrat is keeping watch before the gates of Barad-dûr. You should confront Ushgrat and fight your way out of Barad-dûr.\n17\tEscape from Barad-dûr and find a way out of Mordor!\tLethi and Vaski have drawn Ushgrat's attention away from you. You must escape from Barad-dûr before it is too late! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n18\tEscape from Barad-dûr and find a way out of Mordor!\tYou must escape from Barad-dûr before it is too late!\n19\tTalk to Nagli\tNagli can be found at the Rusted Gate in Ered Luin. After you told the Dourhands of your escape from Mordor, a dwarf named Nagli has asked to speak with you. You should talk to Nagli.\n20\tFollow Nagli\tNagli can be found at the Rusted Gate in Ered Luin. Nagli has suggested that you ask to seek refuge among the Dourhands in Ered Luin. Lacking the authority to make such a decision, Nagli has asked you to speak to Rethvárd that he might bring you before the Steward of Thorin's Hall.\n21\tTalk to Rethvárd\tRethvárd can be found at the Rusted Gate in Ered Luin. Nagli has brought you before Rethvárd, a Dourhand guard, with the hope that he might grant you an audience with Gormr Doursmith, the Steward of Thorin's Hall. You should talk to Rethvárd.\n22\tTalk to Skorgrím\tSkorgrím Dourhand can be found at the Rusted Gate in Ered Luin. Followed by a significant number of Dourhands, and a deathly-looking Man, Skorgrím has asked to speak with you. You should talk to Skorgrím.\n23\tRemain on guard\tSkorgrím, and many of the Dourhands who now follow him, are marching from the Rusted Gate. You should remain on guard.\n24\tDourhands can be found at the Rusted Gate in Ered Luin. Skorgrím Dourhand claims to have been resurrected by a deathly-looking Man called Ivar the Blood-hand, and he has summoned all loyal Dourhands into the service of Angmar. However, a few have hesitated to answer his summons. You should warn them not to follow Skorgrím.\t\n25\tWarn Rethvárd not to follow Skorgrím\tRethvárd can be found at the Rusted Gate in Ered Luin. None of the other Dourhands you warned could be swayed from following Skorgrím. You should warn Rethvárd.\n26\tTalk to Nagli\tNagli can be found at the Rusted Gate in Ered Luin. All of the Dourhands save for Nagli have left with Skorgrím. You should talk to Nagli.\n27\tTalk to Nagli in Thorin's Hall\tNagli has told you of a dwarf named Dwalin, who led the recent Longbeard expedition to Thorin's Hall. Hoping to learn the truth of Skorgrím's claims and seek refuge, Nagli has asked you to travel with him to Thorin's Hall.\n28\tFind Dwalin, the leader of the Longbeard expedition, in Thorin's Hall\tDwalin can be found somewhere within Thorin's Hall. After entering Thorin's Hall, the Longbeards have kept a close watch on Nagli. You should find and speak to Dwalin.\n29\tTalk to Dwalin\tDwalin can be found in Thorin's Hall. You have found Dwalin deep within Thorin's Hall. You should speak to him on behalf of Nagli and plead for refuge in Thorin's Hall.\n",
[7338]="7002FECD\n1\tTalk to Ides\tIdes can be found waiting along the road. Ides wishes to speak with you about hunting the wild bears.\n2\tTalk to Ides\tIdes has ventured with you into the woods. Ides wishes to speak with you about the hunt.\n3\tDefeat the Uruk-hai scouts\tThe Uruk-hai scouts have invaded the woods by the training grounds. Uruks have begun to attack Ides while searching for the location of the training grounds.\n4\tTalk to Ides\tIdes has ventured with you into the woods. Ides wishes to speak with you about the Uruk-hai.\n",
[7339]="7006EEDC\n1\tJoin Mizâdi around the war table\tJoin Mizâdi around the war table.\n2\tListen to the conversation\tListen to the conversation.\n3\tSpeak with Mizâdi\tSpeak with Mizâdi in the war room.\n4\tGather the map from near the Subuzûri\tGather the map from near the Subuzûri.\n5\tSpread the map out on the table\tSpread the map out on the table.\n6\tListen to the conversation\tListen to the conversation.\n7\tListen to the conversation\tListen to the conversation.\n8\tSpeak with Mizâdi in the hall\tSpeak with Mizâdi in the hall.\n",
[7340]="7001627B\n1\tDefeat siege-weapon teams ([see journal]/4)\tWhile the Elves are skilled warriors capable of easily fending off the Dunlendings' assaults, the siege-engines in the field have them pinned down and are dwindling their numbers. You must take to the field, find the siege-engines, and defeat their crews, buying respite for the Elven defenders.\n2\tDefeat the Dunlending commander\tWith his siege-engines out of commission and his assault faltering, the Dunlending commander is leading a final attack against the bridge. He must be stopped.\n3\tUse the ancient anvil\030Collect Infused Sapphire\tHaving defeated the Dunlendings and routed their forces, you may now use the ancient forge to empower your infused sapphire with the blessings of the Elves.\n4\tSpeak with Perimbant to return to Echad Dúnann.\t\n",
[7341]="7007213D\n1\tTalk to Razâl\tRazâl is standing by to begin the infiltration plan. You should talk to Razâl when you are ready to begin.\n2\tEnter the secret cave system\tRazâl is with you and ready to begin. You should enter the secret cave system.\n3\tFind the entrance to the gate-house\tYou and Razâl must find a way into the gate-house to open the gates of Emax Dûl. You should explore the caves with Razâl and find the entrance to the gate-house.\n4\tDefeat the guards in the gate-house\tYou have found the gate-house. You should defeat the guards in the gate-house before they can signal the alarm.\n5\tUse the gate lever\tYou have successfully taken control of the gate-house. You should find and use the lever for the main gate.\n6\tExit the gate-house\tMizâdi's forces have begun the invasion of the city. You should exit the gate-house to the streets of Emax Dûl.\n7\tFind Mizâdi\tMizâdi's forces are fighting for control of Emax Dûl. You should find Mizâdi somewhere up ahead.\n8\tDefeat Góramul Sai\tMizâdi has cornered Góramul Sai at the steps to the palace. You should help your allies defeat Góramul Sai.\n",
[7342]="7004137C\n1\tTalk to Sterkist beside Grimbeorn's pond\tYou and your brother Sterkist have spent many idle afternoons watching the still waters of the pond by Grimbeorn's lodge once the work was done. Sterkist is in a philosophical mood this particular afternoon and wishes to continue your conversation.\n2\tTalk to Sterkist in front of Grimbeorn's lodge\tThe Wizard Radagast has come to Grimbeorn's lodge, and your mind races to determine the reason. Your brother Sterkist wants your help to learn what has brought the Wizard from his Mirkwood home.\n3\tTalk to Varthmath at the animal pen west of Grimbeorn's lodge\tVarthmath may know what brought Radagast out of Mirkwood, and you should find him at the animal pen to the west of the lodge. Your cousin is a man of few words, but his keen ears miss little.\n4\tFind the meandering milk-cow and convince her to return to her pen\tOne of the milk-cows has wandered out of the pen, and Varthmath wants you to find her and send her back before she leaves Grimbeorn's yard.\n5\tTalk to Ofolmóth and learn what he wants from you\tOfolmóth has called your name. He is standing just beyond the gate of Grimbeorn's yard.\n6\tSpeak to Ofolmóth when you are ready to engage in battle with him\tOfolmóth believes that the line of Beorn is best served by constant and ferocious battle. He wants to ensure that you are as strong as you can be, and wants you to test your skills against him in battle. He has asked you to speak to him when you are ready.\n7\tDefeat sickle-flies outside the surrounding fence (total: 8)\tOfolmóth wants you to test your mettle against the sickle-flies around the surrounding fence. If you work your way around the fence to the west and south, you will find the nuisances in sufficient numbers to get some good practice.\n8\tTalk to Langhár in the fields outside Grimbeorn's yard, to the south-west\tYour sister Langhár often wanders the clover-fields, keeping a watch on any threats that stray too near to Grimbeorn's home. She called to you after you defeated many sickle-flies, and she can be found to the south-west.\n9\tHurry back to the entrance to Grimbeorn's lodge\tGoblins have come to the vales of the Anduin, and you should return to Grimbeorn's lodge and warn your family of the threat.\n10\tHurry to Grimbeorn's lodge to warn him of the goblins\tGoblins have come to the vales of the Anduin, and you should bring word of their presence to Grimbeorn at his lodge.\n11\tTalk to Sterkist outside Grimbeorn's lodge\tGoblins have converged on Grimbeorn's yard, and you should bring word to him of their attack.\n12\tListen to Radagast's tidings of the wider world\tIt seems that Radagast already knew of the goblin-movements, and his visit to Grimbeorn related in some way to the rising troubles of the world.\n13\tTalk to Grimbeorn\tGrimbeorn has made his decision: he will send you on Radagast's errand, to bring a warning of the rising darkness that threatens Middle-earth.\n14\tTalk to Radagast\tRadagast has an urgent errand for you to undertake, and it will take you far from the familiar lands of your home.\n15\tTalk to Sterkist and convince him not to remain a sulking bear\030Talk to Langhár\tThe time has come to bid farewell to your siblings before you journey out into the wider world.\n16\tTalk to Radagast and Grimbeorn, fill the horse's saddlebags, and depart on your journey\tYou will need some supplies if you are to have success on your journey.\n",
[7343]="70060D83\n1\tTalk to Fredegar\tTalk to Fredegar.\n2\tThrow stink-bombs at Lotho's Bounders (total: 6)\tThrow stink-bombs at Lotho's Bounders.\n3\tLet events transpire\tLet events transpire.\n4\tDefeat the ruffians\tDefeat the ruffians.\n5\tLet events transpire\tLet events transpire.\n",
[7344]="70052B17\n1\tTalk to Atta\tAtta has offered to tell you his tale of Úbil the Snatcher. You should talk to Atta.\n2\tListen to Atta and follow along with his tale\tAtta is telling you his tale of Úbil the Snatcher. You should listen to Atta as he tells his tale.\n3\tTalk to Atta\tAtta is telling you his tale of Úbil the Snatcher. You should talk to Atta before allowing him to continue his tale.\n4\tTalk to Atta\tAtta is telling you his tale of Úbil the Snatcher. You should talk to Atta.\n5\tListen to Atta and follow along with his tale\tAtta is telling you his tale of Úbil the Snatcher. You should listen to Atta as he tells his tale.\n6\tTalk to Atta\tAtta is telling you his tale of Úbil the Snatcher. You should talk to Atta.\n7\tTalk to Atta\tAtta is telling you his tale of Úbil the Snatcher. You should talk to Atta.\n8\tListen to Atta and follow along with his tale\tAtta is telling you his tale of Úbil the Snatcher. You should listen to Atta as he tells his tale.\n9\tTalk to Atta\tAtta is telling you his tale of Úbil the Snatcher. You should talk to Atta.\n",
[7345]="7003521A\n1\tTalk to the Uruk standing in the road\tA cold wind blows from the north-west of town. You should speak to the Uruk in the north-west of Byre Tor.\n2\tDefeat the Uruk scout\tA cold wind blows from the north-west of town. You should speak to the Uruk in the north-west of Byre Tor.\n3\tTry to escape Byre Tor by heading north-west\tTwo more uruks stand in the road in north-west Byre Tor.\n4\tRun along the road, away from Núrzum\tRun away from Núrzum! You should approach the glowing path markers.\n5\tDefeat attackers (total: 2)\tUruks approach from behind! You should defeat the attacking Uruks.\n6\tRun away from Núrzum, east!\tNúrzum is close behind! You should run in the opposite direction.\n7\tDefeat attackers (total: 2)\tUruks approach from behind! You should defeat the attacking Uruks.\n8\tRun east!\tRun east, away from Núrzum's forces!\n9\tRun north\tRun north, to the edge of Byre Tor.\n10\tJump off the cliff\tJump off the edge of Byre Tor's cliff.\n",
[7346]="70048BFB\n1\tTalk to Rathnor by the waggons\030Talk to Mithrandir south-east of the waggons\030Talk to Linadar west of the waggons\tThe waggons have stopped for the night, and the folk that travel with you prepare to rest.\n2\tTalk to Ayorzén south-west of the waggons\tAyorzén is looking at the sunset not far from where the waggons have stopped for the night.\n3\tSit by the camp-fire near the waggons\tThe men have called for you to sit by the fire with them.\n4\tListen to the conversation by the camp-fire and remain alert\tA brief respite on the way to Minas Tirith will be welcomed by all.\n5\tTalk to Ayorzén by the camp-fire before the situation worsens\tTensions run high by the side of the road where the waggons to Minas Tirith have stopped for the night, and you should try and defuse the situation, if you can.\n6\tListen to the conversation by the camp-fire and remain alert\tTensions run high by the side of the road where the waggons to Minas Tirith have stopped for the night.\n7\tTalk to Linadar by the camp-fire\tLinadar is by the camp-fire near where the waggons have stopped for the night.\n8\tTalk to Mithrandir south-east of the camp-fire\tMithrandir is near the fire where the waggons have stopped for the night.\n",
[7347]="700537B8\n1\tTalk to Vëamacil\tVëamacil is at Díngarth.\n2\tTalk to Ornaher\tOrnaher is at Díngarth.\n3\tTalk to Tárandil\tTárandil is at Díngarth.\n4\tSit by the fire\tThe sons of Isildur wait for you to sit by their camp-fire and share a meal.\n5\tListen to the sons of Isildur discuss the war's progress\tThe sons of Isildur are sharing a meal and conversation around a camp-fire at the encampment of Díngarth.\n6\tTalk to Tárandil\tTárandil has returned with the wine, but he is displeased to be the subject of his foster-brothers' gibes.\n7\tListen to the conversation of the sons of Isildur\tVëamacil and Ornaher are at Díngarth, relating stories told by their eldest brother Meldaran, who remained at the Black Gate.\n8\tTalk to Ornaher\tOrnaher is at Díngarth.\n9\tTalk to the Gondorian soldier\tA Gondorian soldier has interrupted the merry-making to ask a concerning question of the sons of Isildur.\n10\tListen to the sons of Isildur discuss the Ghâzab Bôron, the Storm of Wrath\tA soldier of Gondor has asked the sons of Isildur for tidings of the Ghâzab Bôron.\n11\tTalk to Ornaher\tOrnaher is at Díngarth.\n",
[7348]="70037DBA\n1\tTalk to Herubrand inside Orlag Den\tHerubrand is inside Orlag Den, the cave of the soothsayer Hildegard.\n2\tTalk to Hildegard in Orlag Den\tHildegard is inside the cave of Orlag Den, where she makes her home.\n3\tAnswer Hildegard's questions, and hear what she has to say\tHildegard has asked you what adventuring discipline you follow.\n4\tAnswer Hildegard's questions, and hear what she has to say\tHorn has made his disbelief of Hildegard most plain.\n5\tListen to the words of Hildegard\tHildegard has asked to speak with Nona.\n6\tTalk to Horn in Orlag Den\tHorn is in Orlag Den, the cave of the soothsayer Hildegard.\n7\tListen to Horn and Hildegard's confrontation\tListen to Horn's confrontation with Hildegard in Orlag Den.\n8\tTalk to Nona in Orlag Den\tNona is in Orlag Den, the cave of the soothsayer Hildegard.\n9\tHildegard stands, unblinking, but does not appear to see you any longer\tHildegard stares sightlessly forward.\n10\tTalk to Hildegard in Orlag Den\tHildegard stands, unblinking, but does not appear to see you or Nona any longer.\n",
[7349]="70071CEF\n1\tInvestigate the strange mechanism near the wall of the Blade-horn\tInvestigate the strange mechanism in the torch near the wall of the Blade-horn.\n2\tPress further into the Blade-horn\tPress further into the Blade-horn, behind the broken wall.\n3\tDefeat the attacking spirits (total: 6)\tDefeat the attacking spirits!\n4\tAttempt to calm the mysterious spirit\tAttempt to calm the mysterious spirit within the Blade-horn.\n5\tDefeat the mysterious spirit within the Blade-horn\tDefeat the mysterious spirit within the Blade-horn.\n6\tInvestigate the strange wall within the Blade-horn\tInvestigate the strange crack left by the wailing spirit within the Blade-horn.\n",
[7350]="70071D81\n1\tGet close to the first secret door inside the Blade-horn\tGet close to the first secret door inside the Blade-horn.\n2\tExamine the suspicious wall the spirit went through in the Blade-horn\tExamine the suspicious wall the spirit went through in the Blade-horn.\n3\tFight off the spirits (total: 8)\tDefeat the angry spirits within the passage!\n4\tJoin Khaljûn at the tomb at the end of the corridor\tJoin Khaljûn at the tomb at the end of the corridor.\n5\tListen to the conversation\tListen to the conversation between Khaljûn and the mysterious man.\n6\tListen to the conversation between Khaljûn and Valrazâr\tListen to the conversation between Khaljûn and Valrazâr.\n7\tListen to the conversation between Khaljûn and Valrazâr\tListen to the conversation between Khaljûn and Valrazâr.\n8\tDefeat Valrazâr in the crypt\tDefeat Valrazâr in the crypt.\n9\tListen to Khaljûn in the crypt of the Blade-horn\tListen to Khaljûn in the crypt of the Blade-horn.\n10\tListen to Khaljûn in the crypt of the Blade-horn\t\n",
[7351]="70041382\n1\tTalk to Clothar in the Old Forest\tClothar Sandheaver is in the Old Forest, and is not very happy about it.\n2\tTalk to the new arrival in the language of animals\tClothar has been startled by the sudden appearance of an animal, but it is merely a skittish deer, and not the giant bear he expected. You should speak to it in the language of animals, and learn if it has seen the maddened bear.\n3\tTalk to Clothar in the Old Forest\tYou encountered a skittish deer in the Old Forest and learned that a predator is near. Could it be the giant bear that Clothar Sandheaver encountered?\n4\tDefeat the great bear\tYou have found the bear that menaced Clothar and filled him with fear!\n5\tTalk to the great bear in the language of his kind\tThe bear is enormous and seems driven to frenzy, but still you see something in its eye that gives you pause.\n6\tFight the great bear, but do not slay him\tYou have found the bear that menaced Clothar and filled him with fear! It seemed as if you almost calmed the great bear with your words, but the creature shook away your influence.\n7\tTalk to the great bear in the language of his kind\tYou have seen fear in the eyes of the great bear, and are now certain: something against its nature has driven this creature to attack.\n8\tYou have learned the name of the great bear, Bramblesnarl, and that some evil has put a great and terrible fear into the creature, causing it to become frenzied.\t\n9\tTalk to Bramblesnarl in the language of his kind\tThe fear is gone, and now in Bramblesnarl's eyes you see something else: respect, and admiration. You have saved the bear from himself.\n10\tTalk to Clothar in the Old Forest\tClothar Sandheaver is in the Old Forest, and can hardly believe his eyes or his ears.\n",
[7352]="70015790\n1\tRescue cocooned dwarves (total: 6)\030Defeat the crystal brood-mother\tYou must rescue the dwarves cocooned within the ancient armoury before they are devoured by the ravenous hatchlings from the nest.\n2\tUse the ancient anvil\030Collect Infused Adamant\tUse the ancient forge to empower your infused adamant.\n",
[7353]="70066DBB\n1\tTalk to Byrski Hardprow\tByrski Hardprow has sailed the Saervig onto the Mirrormere.\n2\tLook off the larboard side of the Saervig and search for Durin's Crown\tLarboard can be found on the left side of a ship, when facing toward the bow. Byrski Hardprow has asked you to look off the larboard side of the Saervig and search for Durin's Crown.\n3\tLook off the starboard side of the Saervig and search for Durin's Crown\tStarboard can be found on the right side of a ship, when facing toward the bow. Byrski Hardprow has asked you to look off the starboard side of the Saervig and search for Durin's Crown.\n4\tLook off the stern of the Saervig and search for Durin's Crown\tThe stern can be found at the rear or aft of the Saervig. Byrski Hardprow has asked you to look off the stern of the Saervig and search for Durin's Crown.\n5\tLook off the bow of the Saervig and search for Durin's Crown\tThe bow can be found at the front or fore of the Saervig. Byrski Hardprow has asked you to look off the bow of the Saervig and search for Durin's Crown.\n6\tTalk to Byrski Hardprow\tByrski Hardprow has sailed the Saervig onto the Mirrormere. You have looked for Durin's Crown in several places, but your search has not been successful. You should talk to Byrski Hardprow.\n7\tLook for the glint in the Mirrormere\tThe glint that Byrski spotted can be found off the starboard side of the Saervig, nearer to its bow. Byrski Hardprow has asked you to look for the glint he saw in the Mirrormere and tell him if you also believe it to be Durin's Crown.\n8\tCould this be the light of the Star of Eärendil?\tYou have been engulfed in a brilliant, white light, and though you cannot identify the light's source, its warmth lifts your spirit.\n9\tTalk to Byrski Hardprow\tByrski Hardprow has sailed the Saervig onto the Mirrormere. You have been engulfed in a curious light, but Byrski appears concerned. You should talk to Byrski Hardprow.\n",
[7354]="70057613\n1\tPlace the Secret Stone on its pedestal\tThe time has finally come. You must place the Secret Stone on the fifth pedestal.\n2\tKill Frethi\tSomething is wrong. What just happened? You should talk to Frethi.\n3\tWitness the release of the Shadowed King\tHe has been released! Witness his might!\n",
[7355]="700303CA\n1\tTalk to Éomer by the Stone of Wyrgende\tÉomer has come to the Stone of Wyrgende, but you have not entirely divined his purpose for doing so. You should speak to Éomer to learn why he has come to this grim place before continuing on to Snowbourn.\n2\tTalk to Éomer at the Stone of Wyrgende\tÉomer is at the Stone of Wyrgende.\n3\tTalk to Corudan at the Stone of Wyrgende\030Talk to Horn at the Stone of Wyrgende\tHorn and Corudan are at Wyrgende's Stone.\n4\tDefeat Vale-scouts (total: 6)\tOrcs are attacking the area near Wyrgende's Stone!\n5\tTalk to Éomer at the Stone of Wyrgende\tÉomer is at the Stone of Wyrgende.\n",
[7356]="7006B06E\n1\tDefeat ambushers\tFight off the ambush awaiting you in Rothog's chambers.\n2\tSpeak to Rothog the Storm and watch his reaction\tArmed with proof of Shaidal's innocence, you approach Rothog the Storm with your findings.\n3\tSpeak to Shaidal about his task\tSpeak to Shaidal about his task.\n",
[7357]="70034B8F\n1\tListen to Iothete\tIothete is in his hut in the Whitshaws. You should speak with Iothete.\n2\tListen to Iothete's tale\tIothete is in the woods of the Whitshaws. You should speak with Iothete and listen to his memory of a fateful day.\n3\tListen to Iothete's tale\tIothete is in the woods of the Whitshaws. You should speak with Iothete and listen to his memory of a fateful day.\n4\tFollow Iothete\tIothete is in the woods in the northern Whitshaws. You should speak with Iothete.\n5\tTalk to Iothete\tIothete is in the woods in the northern Whitshaws. You should speak with Iothete.\n6\tListen to Iothete\tYou should follow Iothete's memory into his home in Dunfast.\n7\tListen to Iothete's memory\tYou should follow Iothete's memory into his home in Dunfast.\n8\tListen to Iothete's memory\tYou should follow Iothete's memory into his home in Dunfast.\n9\tTalk to Iothete\tYou should follow Iothete's memory into his home in Dunfast.\n",
[7358]="70059AF5\n1\tTalk to Mótsog and hear his tale\tMótsog's tale is nearly complete.\n2\tHear the tale of Mótsog\tMótsog's tale is nearly complete.\n3\tTalk to Mótsog and hear his tale\tMótsog's tale is nearly complete.\n4\tClimb the stairs to Biriz-zahar\tThe army led by Ragna the Fierce climbed the unguarded stairs to the high places of Biriz-zahar.\n5\tTalk to Mótsog and hear his tale\tMótsog's tale is nearly complete.\n6\tHear the tale of Mótsog\tMótsog's tale is nearly complete.\n7\tTalk to Mótsog and hear his tale\tMótsog's tale is nearly complete.\n8\tFollow Ragna the Fierce through the burning city\tRagna the Fierce renewed her attempt to rescue her husband and king.\n9\tFollow Ragna the Fierce through the burning city\tMótsog speaks of Sauron's betrayal of the Greymauls, and of Ragna's race through the blood-drenched city of Biriz-zahar.\n10\tTalk to Mótsog atop Biriz-zahar\tMótsog continues his tale of the Sunder-battle.\n11\tHear the tale of Mótsog\tMótsog's tale is nearly complete.\n",
[7359]="700539F5\n1\tTalk to Gandalf in the Halls of Memory\tGandalf speaks to you of the discoveries he made while studying the Black Book.\n2\tReturn to the Grey Mountains, as depicted by the Halls of Memory\tGandalf wishes to resume the tale of Vóin in the Grey Mountains as they are depicted by the Halls of Memory.\n3\tTalk to Gandalf in the Grey Mountains as depicted by the Halls of Memory\tGandalf is in the Grey Mountains, as depicted by the Halls of Memory.\n4\tMove through the twisting passage until you reach another of the Halls of Memory\tFurther information about Vóin's journey to Gondor as one of Eärnur's boon companions lies beyond the Grey Mountains, in the Halls of Memory.\n5\tApproach the band of adventurers in the tavern depicted by the Halls of Memory\tVóin and his companions met at a tavern in Minas Anor one night, and planned a dangerous excursion.\n6\tListen to the account of Vóin and his friends at the tavern depicted by the Halls of Memory\tVóin and his companions met at a tavern in Minas Anor one night, and planned a dangerous excursion.\n7\tTalk to Gandalf in the Minas Anor tavern depicted by the Halls of Memory\tGandalf is in the tavern depicted by the Halls of Memory.\n8\tMove through the twisting passage to another of the Halls of Memory\tGandalf's study of the Black Book has revealed an excursion by Eärnur and his companions to recapture the fortress of Durthang, in Gorgoroth.\n9\tTalk to Gandalf in Durthang as depicted by the Halls of Memory\tGandalf is in Durthang, as depicted by the Halls of Memory.\n10\tListen to the account of Eärnur's doomed adventure within Durthang\tGandalf's study of the Black Book has revealed an excursion by Eärnur and his companions to recapture the fortress of Durthang, in Gorgoroth.\n11\tTalk to Gandalf in Durthang as depicted by the Halls of Memory\tGandalf is in Durthang, as depicted by the Halls of Memory.\n12\tListen to the conclusion of Eärnur's doomed adventure within Durthang\tGandalf's study of the Black Book has revealed an excursion by Eärnur and his companions to recapture the fortress of Durthang, in Gorgoroth.\n13\tTalk to Gandalf in Durthang as depicted by the Halls of Memory\tGandalf is in Durthang, as depicted by the Halls of Memory.\n",
[7360]="700442F0\n1\tInvestigate the slain Sûhalar\tNearby is another slain body. You should investigate the slain Sûhalar.\n2\tExamine the bear trap\tThere is a bear trap on the slain body. You should examine the bear trap.\n3\tSearch nearby for another sign of this Sûhalar slayer\tThe Sûhalar slayer must be nearby. You should search nearby for more signs of conflict.\n4\tExamine the foot prints\tThere are footprints around the slain body. You should examine foot prints.\n5\tLet the events transpire\tLet the events transpire.\n6\tRun after Tolwin so that you may speak with him\tYou should run after Tolwin so that you may speak with him.\n7\tSpeak with Tolwin\tYou should speak with Tolwin.\n8\tLet Tolwin tell his story\tLet Tolwin tell his story.\n9\tSpeak with Tolwin\tYou should speak with Tolwin.\n",
})
